  "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirement\nThe task was to find the software requirements for iPhones that support AirDrop's ability to continue transmitting over the web (internet) when out of range.\n\n## Screenshot Analysis\n\n**Screenshot 1:** Shows a Google search page with the query \"AirDrop continue transfer over internet when out of range iPhone software requirements\" entered — an appropriate search for the task.\n\n**Screenshot 2:** Shows the Google search results with an AI Overview that explicitly states: *\"Continuing an AirDrop transfer over the internet or cellular data when moving out of range requires **iOS 17.1 or later** on your iPhone.\"* It further details the Software & System Requirements, listing \"Operating System: iOS 17.1 or later installed on both iPhones (or iPadOS 17.1+ / macOS 14.1+ equivalents).\" Below, an Apple Support result (\"Use AirDrop to send items to nearby Apple devices\") includes the snippet: \"If you leave Bluetooth or Wi-Fi range after an AirDrop transfer is initiated, the transfer continues over the internet.\"\n\n**Screenshots 3–5:** Show the official Apple iPhone User Guide (iOS 17) page titled \"Use AirDrop on iPhone to send items to nearby Apple devices,\" which contains the note: *\"If you leave Bluetooth or Wi-Fi range after an AirDrop transfer is initiated, the transfer continues over the internet.\"* This confirms the feature described in the task.\n\n## Response Analysis\nThe response states the software requirement is **iOS 17.1 or later**, citing the Apple iPhone User Guide. This aligns with the Google AI Overview visible in Screenshot 2, which explicitly states iOS 17.1 or later is required. The Apple User Guide screenshots corroborate the feature's existence (transfer continues over the internet when out of Bluetooth/Wi-Fi range).\n\n## Conclusion\nThe agent performed a relevant search, located authoritative information (Google AI Overview and Apple's official User Guide), and correctly identified the software requirement (iOS 17.1 or later). The answer in the response is directly supported by the screenshot content. The task's objective — finding the software requirement — was fully accomplished.\n\n**Verdict: SUCCESS**",
